title: Proxmox Node Swap Usage
agents: linux
catalog: os/kernel
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the overall swap usage of a Proxmox VE node and
 identifies the virtual machines (QEMU) and containers (LXC) that are
 responsible for the host swap being consumed.

 The service state is derived from configurable warning/critical levels on
 the percentage of the node's total swap that is in use. The summary lists
 the top swap-consuming guests; the details view lists the top ten guests
 plus a swap accounting breakdown (guests vs. host/system).

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {proxmox_node_swap}, which reads
 {/proc/meminfo}, the cgroup v2 values under {/sys/fs/cgroup/lxc/} and the
 {VmSwap} of the running QEMU processes. The plug-in can be deployed via the
 Agent Bakery.

 Levels can be configured with the rule "Proxmox node swap usage".

item:
 None.

discovery:
 One service {Proxmox Node Swap Usage} is created on every host that sends
 the {proxmox_node_swap} agent section.
